Yes: binary-partition the shorter array in \(O(\log\min(m,n))\) time and \(O(1)\) space.
```python
def median_two_sorted(a,b):
    if len(a)>len(b): return median_two_sorted(b,a)
    if not b: raise ValueError('empty input')
    m,n=len(a),len(b); half=(m+n+1)//2; lo,hi=0,m
    while lo<=hi:
        i=(lo+hi)//2; j=half-i
        al=a[i-1] if i else float('-inf'); ar=a[i] if i<m else float('inf')
        bl=b[j-1] if j else float('-inf'); br=b[j] if j<n else float('inf')
        if al<=br and bl<=ar:
            left=max(al,bl)
            return left if (m+n)%2 else (left+min(ar,br))/2
        if al>br: hi=i-1
        else: lo=i+1
    raise ValueError('inputs not sorted')
```

